{"type": "thinking", "text": "Reproduced: replace produced \"(A) Fee rent\\n2026-11-14 \". So there's an unwanted \"2026-11-14 \" inserted on a new line. This is consistent and reproducible.\n\nWait — but is this maybe expected Markor behavior? No. Replace should only replace matches. Extra date text is definitely wrong.\n\nWhere does \"2026-11-14 \" come from? Possibly the replace dialog shares a layout with the \"insert date\" dialog and a hidden field got applied. Or maybe the \"shared layout\" bug: the EditText in the shared layout has `android:freezesText` or something carrying over a previously entered date. Hmm. Actually! The date \"2026-11-14\" is what was inserted by the Toggle done earlier. But how would that be retained? Unless the editor's undo/redo buffer is buggy... Hmm.\n\nLet's test: undo fully, then type something manually (not toggle done), then do a replace, and see if \"2026-11-14\" still appears. If it appears even after typing, then it's from replace itself, not leftover. Let's check: Currently text \"(A) Fee rent\\n2026-11-14 \". Hit undo once → back to \"(A) Pay rent\\n\". Then type \"q\" at end? Hmm, that changes. Better: undo, then close and reopen file, then do replace.\n\nActually simpler: undo now. Then navigate away and reopen todo.txt, verify text, then do replace again. If the extra date appears, likely date comes from replace's shared layout (maybe the replace field prefilled? no, it showed \"Replace with\" empty).\n\nHmm wait, maybe I should reconsider. In Markor, the search-replace dialog \"Replace with\" field might have an \"insert date\" button? No.\n\nAlternatively, the extra line could come from the \"date\" auto-insertion when the dialog closes? Unlikely.\n\nActually, is it possible that \"2026-11-14 \" is the *current clipboard* content and the replace input field was sharing state with clipboard? No.\n\nHold on, let me reconsider whether the extra line is caused by the *replace text* itself being applied twice: \"Fee\" appears once, fine.\n\nLet me look at what the replace operation does in Markor source (memory): `SearchReplaceDialog` uses `search_input` and `replace_input` EditTexts. On replace, it calls `editor.getText().replace(...)`. It would only insert replace string at match. So extra date is weird.\n\nUnless... the shared layout has a third hidden EditText (e.g., from the \"insert date\" dialog) that is also bound, and its text \"2026-11-14\" gets appended? Hmm.\n\nLet me test with a different doc (Regex.md) which has never had toggle done. Do replace there and see whether extra date appears. If it does, then it's the replace bug. If not, the date is leftover somehow.\n\nLet me undo now, go to Regex.md via Files."}
