{"type": "thinking", "text": "Undo restores original. This confirms it's an inserted change.\n\nNow I need to understand enough to report. The bug: Search & Replace in this dialog inserts \"2026-11-14 \" (today's date) on a new line at the end of the document when replacing.\n\nWait... Actually now I suspect the \"2026-11-14 \" might be the current *date* itself because the shared layout's EditText fields are reusing the layout of an \"insert date\" dialog and the dialog's \"Choose format\" spinner. Hmm. The recent_show_spinner \"Choose format\" maybe is the date format selector? Hmm, \"Choose format\" could be for date format indeed. The spinner at y=550 between the two fields. If it's the date format spinner, then the dialog's result includes a date insert? Hmm, maybe this dialog is Markor's \"Search / Replace\" where \"Choose format\" is for \"recent search format\"? Unclear.\n\nRegardless, the observed behavior is wrong. But let me double-check that \"2026-11-14 \" extra is not because of some intentional \"move task to done date\" logic in todo.txt search-replace. Unlikely.\n\nLet me test the same dialog with an empty replace string (delete) to see if extra date appears. And test with the \"Regex\" checkbox. Also test \"Replace all\". But before that, I realize the extra date may be a genuine separate injection: maybe the shared layout has a third EditText with default text \"2026-11-14\" that's accidentally included? But the dialog only shows 2 fields.\n\nWait, maybe the date is from the *cursor position / current date insertion*: In Markor's search/replace dialog, when it builds the fields from a shared layout, perhaps it mistakenly uses the `date` format text as the initial text of the replace field, but we clearly saw replace field empty. Hmm.\n\nActually! Maybe the appended text \"2026-11-14 \" is produced by the todo.txt's \"date and time\" helper. Could the \"Replace\" action in this dialog be implemented by simulating key events? Eh.\n\nLet's test on a non-todo file. Can we get this dialog in Regex.md? Earlier in Regex.md the Search button opened the in-editor find bar, not this dialog. So this dialog may be only for todo.txt. Hmm, but \"Search documents\" title... Maybe there's another route: From Files browser, tap Search (element 3) — that might open this \"Search documents\" dialog (search across documents) regardless of current file. Let's test later.\n\nActually, maybe the reason is: the todo.txt editor is opened in \"To-Do\" tab? No, we opened from Files. The toolbar title \"todo\". Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe Markor decides: if file is todo.txt, search uses a different dialog. Fine.\n\nNow, the changed areas: todo.txt files; editor settings; search and replace. This bug fits \"search and replace\" (the dialog). Good.\n\nBut is the extra date maybe the *done-prefix constant* being applied wrongly in search/replace? The changed \"done prefix built from one constant template\" might be used in this search/replace dialog too (e.g., replacing in todo.txt?). Hmm! Interesting: maybe the \"Search / Replace\" dialog for todo.txt applies a \"date\" to the replacement, and the shared template constant leaks. But the date 2026-11-14 is today's date. Hmm.\n\nActually hold on. Maybe the extra line \"2026-11-14 \" is the result of the replace function itself being fed the *replacement string twice*? no.\n\nLet me look at what \"Choose format\" spinner does. Maybe it's \"Choose format\" for the replaced text? Clicking it might give options like \"Text\", \"Date\", etc. That could reveal that the dialog deliberately inserts a date. But it's labeled \"Choose format\" and is a spinner at the middle. Hmm, in Markor, there's a dialog for \"Insert date and time\" with format spinner. Maybe the shared layout is shared between the \"Insert date and time\" dialog and the \"Search/Replace\" dialog! And the bug: the date field's text is being inserted when replacing. But that still doesn't explain the mechanism.\n\nOoh, here's a plausible mechanism: The shared layout might contain multiple EditTexts, including one for \"date format\" or \"insert date\" (maybe hidden). In the Search/Replace dialog, both the search field and replace field are added from the shared layout; but the *third* EditText in the layout (date input) is left in the dialog with its text \"2026-11-14\"? No, we saw only two.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the \"Replace (1)\" button's action gets the text from the *date field* incorrectly because of shared layout ids: The replace field and a hidden date field share the same ID, and the date field's text \"2026-11-14\" overrides. But the replacement text observed was \"Fee\" (correct), so not that.\n\nHmm, what if the extra text is added by the dialog's \"recent\" spinner? no.\n\nHonestly, the precise mechanism doesn't matter for reporting; I just need observed vs expected with reproducible steps. But I want to be sure it's a real bug and not an artifact of something I did. Fresh reopen + replace reproduces. Good.\n\nLet me also check the in-editor find/replace for the same issue on a markdown file. Already did Regex.md: no extra date. So the bug is specific to the todo.txt \"Search / Replace\" dialog.\n\nHmm wait, but maybe the todo.txt editor's \"Search documents\" dialog is the *global* file search and the REPLACE dialog is generic. In that case the bug might occur in any file when accessed via this dialog. We can try from the Files browser search route on Regex.md later.\n\nLet me now investigate the other areas: editor settings and typing helpers. Then come back.\n\nNavigation: More tab → Settings (Preferences). Let's go. First restore file state; current doc \"(A) Pay rent\\n\" unsaved? Text equals original, no change. Undo disabled. Fine.\n\nBut wait: the files list earlier showed todo.txt description as \"11/14/2026, 6:33 AM\" — that's a timestamp, not content. Fine.\n\nLet's go to More tab. Press back (hide keyboard) then tap More."}
