ad\" because it was cut. The Tools submenu had only one element \"Speed Read\" at y=262 and maybe more below off-screen? The submenu popup had 2 elements. Hmm, maybe additional items in Tools submenu are below but popup height limited? It showed only \"Speed Read\".\n\nHmm, maybe the typing helpers are exposed in File Settings menu: Wrap Words, Line Numbers, Syntax Highlighting, Auto-format... no.\n\nWait — maybe \"typing helpers\" refers to the \"Special Key\" (keyboard) dialog? In the editor bottom bar, the \"Special Key\" icon (keyboard) opens a dialog with buttons: Tab, arrows, etc. \"Typing helpers\" might be that dialog plus toggles in settings? Hmm.\n\nLet me search the web memory: Markor has \"editor typing helpers\" — I actually recall Markor's settings has \"Typing helpers\" under \"Editor Settings\" maybe? Hmm. But the Edit Mode list we saw: Font, Font Size, Basic color scheme, Syntax Highlighting, Underline Hex Color Codes, Disable spelling underline, Use monospace font for code, Disable highlighting for code blocks, Bigger headings. That's all, no typing helpers. Maybe more items if scrolled, but swipe failed. Let me retry scrolling the Edit Mode list using short swipe x=300,y=2000 distance 0.3 like the successful one. Earlier I tried long swipes which failed. Let's redo.\n\nGo back to Settings → Edit Mode. Currently in todo.txt settings. Press back → Settings, tap Edit Mode (5), then short swipe."}
