{"type": "thinking", "text": "Even with \"Add completion date\" unchecked, toggling done still added \"2026-11-14\"! That's a bug! The setting says \"Add completion date for todos when marking them as done\" — when unchecked, expected \"x Pay rent pri:A\" (no date). But observed \"x 2026-11-14 Pay rent pri:A\".\n\nHmm, but wait: does the setting need an app restart to take effect? In Markor, AppSettings values are read at runtime; the toggle applies trivially. The changed area says \"done prefix built from one constant template\" — maybe the constant always includes date, ignoring the setting. This is very likely the injected bug in the todo.txt area!\n\nBut let me verify that the setting is indeed saved and not still checked. Reopen settings to confirm the checkbox is unchecked after app navigation. Actually I did uncheck it and then navigate; the checkbox element disappeared (unchecked). Good.\n\nAlso, maybe the setting only affects the \"done\" action when the \"date\" format is configured... Let me double-check the setting label: \"Add completion date for todos when marking them as done\". Yes. Unchecked → no date should be added. Observed date added. This is a clear bug.\n\nHmm, but wait — maybe Markor's behavior when the setting is off: The done prefix is \"x \" without date, but the template constant used is \"x %s \" and they pass an empty string, resulting in \"x \" double space? The observed is \"x 2026-11-14 \" — so it's ignoring the setting.\n\nLet me consider: Is the changed item specifically \"the done prefix is now built from one constant template\" — maybe before, the code was `\"x \" + (dateEnabled ? date + \" \" : \"\")`; the refactor to a constant template accidentally always includes the date. That fits perfectly.\n\nLet me confirm persistence of setting and reproduce a second time, then file report. Also, we should determine expected exactly: with \"Add completion date\" off, marking done should add just \"x \" prefix (no date). Let me undo this and test toggling again after confirming setting off.\n\nFirst undo (38)."}
