{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed: \"Add completion date\" has no checkbox (unchecked), \"Append contexts and projects\" checked. So the setting is off but done prefix still has date → bug.\n\nNow let me also confirm expected behavior maybe by toggling on and off again; it's enough. But let me reproduce the mark-done-with-setting-off once more after this navigation (we already did once after setting off, but that was the same session; the setting persisted). Good.\n\nNow file the bug report for this. Need screen/element/field/symptom_type/expected/observed/steps, element_ref and observed_quote from latest observe. The latest observe is the settings screen showing the unchecked setting (elements 3, 4). But the defect is observed in the editor text \"x 2026-11-14 Pay rent pri:A \\n\". The latest observe doesn't include that quote now. The instruction: \"point at the element (element_ref) and quote what the screen shows (observed_quote)... a quote that was never on screen gets the report rejected.\" So for the report, I should be on the screen showing the defect (the editor with the done line) when quoting. Better: reopen todo.txt, toggle done again, capture the observed text, then file report with element_ref of the EditText. Let me do that.\n\nBut also note: the \"done prefix constant\" bug might also manifest with priority, but that's fine.\n\nWait, before that — maybe the expected behavior with date disabled is \"x Pay rent pri:A\" or \"x  Pay rent pri:A\"? Standard todo.txt done prefix is \"x \" (x + space). With no date, line becomes \"x Pay rent pri:A\". We'll state expected \"x Pay rent pri:A\" (no completion date).\n\nLet me reproduce once more and file with element_ref. Navigate back to Files → todo.txt → tap line 1 → toggle done. Also ensure keyboard hidden doesn't matter.\n\nPress back, back, Files, todo.txt, tap line1, toggle."}
