 time\" action being triggered by the keyboard's Enter key**. When I typed \"Fee\" into the replace field, pressing type_text might submit? No submit not set. Hmm.\n\nWait, in this last attempt, before typing, the dialog's \"Search for\" and \"Replace with\" were prefilled? The spinner list shows \"Search for: Pay / Replace with: Fee\" as recent. But when we opened the dialog fresh, fields were empty (\"Search for\"/\"Replace with\" hints). Actually, are they empty? The observe shows EditText \"Search for\" and \"Replace with\" — those could be the *hint text*, not values. In the earlier run, typing \"Pay\" changed it to \"Pay\". So empty initially.\n\nHmm, what if the date insertion is triggered by the **hardware \"Return\" key** being pressed when type_text types into the field? type_text without submit shouldn't.\n\nLet's test with empty replacement on a match, without typing any replacement: Select \"Pay\" search, then tap Replace(1) with empty replace — it should delete \"Pay\". Does date appear? If yes, the date insertion is unconditional. Let's do that: search \"rent\", leave replace empty, tap Replace. But the recent spinner list includes our entries; we can set search \"rent\" by typing.\n\nActually, this exploration costs steps. The developer rejected the report, which means I need a more precise/non-reproducible-proof report or find the actual root. Perhaps the real bug isn't the date line in replace; maybe that's an artifact of the **todo.txt editor's \"date and time\" action with shared layout**. Hmm, but the change list says the search/replace dialog inputs are built from a shared layout, and the bug could indeed be that the **dialog's buttons also trigger another action**. The date insertion is a strong signal.\n\nLet's think about the shared layout: The text says \"Search and replace dialog: the input fields are now built from a shared layout.\" In Markor source, `SearchReplaceDialog` uses a layout `dialog_search_replace.xml` which has a `Spinner` (recent searches) + EditText search + EditText replace. The change \"input fields built from a shared layout\" might mean the two EditTexts are inflated from a common layout `dialog_edittext.xml`. A common injected bug: **hint text swapped** or **the two fields share the same view ID**, causing the search field value to also be in the replace field. Our observations: both fields had independent values (\"Pay\" and \"Fee\"), hints correct. So the fields work.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the replace field's **`inputType`** or **`singleLine`** is wrong: e.g., \"Replace with\" is multi-line so pressing Enter inserted a newline into the replacement, and our replacement string might have ended with newline? But the date line is not newline.\n\nHmm, the date \"2026-11-14 \" is suspicious. Could it be from the clipboard? Did we ever copy \"2026-11-14 \" to clipboard? The toggle done inserted it into the editor; could the IME have learned it as a suggestion? The keyboard suggestion strip showed \"tent/rent/rental\" etc. Hmm! Wait — could \"2026-11-14 \" be an **autocorrect suggestion** that got auto-inserted? No.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it's the **\"Date and time\" action on the bottom bar being tapped accidentally by the tap on the Replace button**? Let's check coordinates: In the dialog, Replace(1) is at (304,972). After tapping, the dialog closes. The touch might be a tap that both activates the dialog button AND, upon the dialog disappearing before the ACTION_UP, the ACTION_UP could hit the underlying editor at (304,972) — that's the editor text area, not the date action. The date action is at (698,1441) — no.\n\nHmm, but wait: the dialog might close on ACTION_DOWN, and the ACTION_UP at (304,972) in the editor... the editor is at that location. A tap there would place the cursor, not insert date. Unless the tap fell on the \"Date and time\" action because the action bar shifted up/down when the dialog closed and keyboard layout changed? The action bar is above the keyboard at y≈1441; not 972. No.\n\nCould the extra date come from **hardware keyboard Enter** triggered by the dialog's positive button (Replace) which after closing the dialog sends an Enter to the editor? Enter would insert \"\\n\", not date. But if the editor has a **\"date and time\" suggestion**? no.\n\nHmm, what if the date string \"2026-11-14 \" is the **current todo.txt completion-date prefix** that the editor's \"auto-format\" inserted when the new line was created? Wait! When the replace operation modifies the todo.txt, maybe Markor's todo.txt \"auto-format\" automatically appends a date to... no.\n\nLet's look at the exact text again: \"(A) Fee rent\\n2026-11-14 \" — note the extra line \"2026-11-14 \" is not a todo task (no \"x\"). It's the bare date. Markor's \"Date and time\" insert action inserts the date in the current date format (yyyy-MM-dd) with a trailing space. So it really is the Date and time action result.\n\nCould the Replace action be bound to the same `onClick` as the \"Date and time\" action due to **shared layout button IDs**? The dialog's positive button is likely `button1` (as in the \"Search documents\" dialog: OK is button1, REPLACE is button3, CANCEL is button2). In the Search/Replace dialog, Replace(1) might be `button1` too. If some code looked up `button1` from the shared layout (which is the date-insert dialog's positive button) and wired it to insertDate, then pressing Replace(1) would insert date. That's plausible in a benchmark-injected bug: \"input fields built from shared layout\" and a callback bound by ID.\n\nBut the developer says couldn't reproduce. Maybe because my sequence involves the *\"Search documents\"* dialog's REPLACE button which is only present in todo.txt's search, and the developer tested the *in-editor find/replace bar* instead. The task says \"Search and replace dialog: the input fields are now built from a shared layout.\" Perhaps the intended dialog is the in-editor find/replace bar (searchEditText/replaceEditText), NOT the \"Search / Replace\" popup. On Regex.md, the in-editor replace worked correctly (cat→dog, no date). But \"search and replace dialog\" more likely refers to the popup dialog with \"Search / Replace\" title. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the correct route to the Search/Replace dialog is from the **file browser search** (not the todo editor search). Let me test that route: File", "truncated": true}
