{"type": "thinking", "text": "Restored to \"(A) Pay rent\\n\". Good.\n\nNow, the Enter→date behavior in todo.txt: Is this a bug? It's suspicious. But the \"changed\" item about typing helpers says \"Editor overflow menu typing helpers: their toggles are now applied directly to the open editor session.\" Perhaps \"typing helpers\" are the toggles in the overflow File Settings, and the injection broke one: maybe \"Auto-format\" toggle now causes Enter to insert a date in todo.txt! Hmm, maybe the \"auto-format\" for todo.txt is supposed to add the current date when you press Enter on a new task — actually YES! Markor's todo.txt **auto-format** might be designed to automatically add a completion date placeholder when creating a new task? Hmm, but the date on an empty line? In todo.txt, a new task line would get a date? No.\n\nHmm, let me check the Markor docs mentally: Markor's \"Auto-format\" (in File Settings) \"Auto-format: Automatically format the text while typing (e.g., continue lists, add list bullets)\". For todo.txt, pressing Enter after a task might create a new line with the current date? Hmm, no.\n\nActually, maybe the date insertion on Enter is because the **\"Add completion date\" setting** is ON. When you create a new task line, the app might add the completion date? No, completion date is for done tasks.\n\nWait, we can test with \"Add completion date\" OFF whether Enter inserts date. That distinguishes. But regardless, the search/replace bug (extra new line with date) still happens; if date insertion on Enter is expected, then the bug is just the extra Enter after replace.\n\nLet me test Enter in Regex.md (markdown) to see if date is todo-specific. If markdown Enter just adds newline, then the date is todo-specific — could be a feature/config. But the replace dialog injecting Enter is still a bug.\n\nGiven the developer rejected the first report, maybe I should file it as a different symptom: \"no_effect\"? no. Let me reconsider whether the extra newline/date might be **expected behavior of the search/replace dialog in todo.txt**? Absolutely not.\n\nMaybe the developer rejection is because they couldn't reproduce *exactly with the steps*, e.g., they might not have the \"Search documents\" dialog path. I should give a simpler repro: \n1. Open todo.txt.\n2. Tap Search icon.\n3. Tap REPLACE.\n4. Type \"Pay\" in Search for, leave \"Replace with\" empty? (Deleting).\n5. Tap Replace.\nResult: extra date line.\n\nI'll re-file with explicit note \"This is the Search / Replace dialog reached via Search → REPLACE (not the in-editor find bar)\". Also mention the keyboard stays open and focus returns to editor with an extra new line.\n\nBut maybe before re-filing, I should determine the actual expected vs observed accurately: The extra content \"2026-11-14 \" is the current date. It appears because the Enter action in todo.txt editor inserts current date into a blank line. Is that Enter behavior intentional? Let me test Enter in Regex2 (markdown) and in todo with Auto-format OFF to understand.\n\nActually, more valuable: test the search/replace dialog on a **markdown file** to see if it also injects an extra newline (without date). If it injects a newline too, then the bug is generic to the dialog (Replace sends Enter), and the date is just todo's Enter-helper. But how to reach the dialog for markdown? The todo Search button is todo-specific. Maybe in the To-Do tab, the search is different. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the Search/Replace dialog is reachable from the **file browser's \"Search\" → \"Search in content\"** flow: search results may offer replace? The Files search dialog had OK only. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the \"Search documents\" dialog is the **To-Do task search** (todo-specific). The \"Search / Replace\" dialog it opens might be a **generic search-replace for the current document**. It may be reachable via the todo editor's search only.\n\nOK. Let me test if Enter in todo.txt inserts the date intentionally by toggling \"Auto-format\" off. If Enter behavior changes, then it's tied to auto-format (a typing helper!). This is directly relevant to the \"typing helpers\" changed area! Maybe the injected bug: the \"Auto-format\" typing helper gained a *date insertion* behavior applied to the open editor session — i.e., pressing Enter inserts the date. Hmm, that could be the actual bug in area #2! But how would \"toggles applied directly to open editor session\" cause Enter to insert date? Maybe the \"Date and time\" action's click handler got bound to the Enter key due to a shared layout? Hmm.\n\nLet's test: Turn OFF Auto-format (overflow → File Settings → Auto-format row), then press Enter in todo.txt. If date no longer appears, Auto-format is responsible. Then turn it back on.\n\nHmm, wait: the date-insert-on-Enter might be an intentional feature of todo.txt **when Auto-format is on**: when you press Enter, it might start a new task with the current date as a header? I doubt.\n\nLet's just test. Open overflow (43), File Settings (0), tap Auto-format (7). Then press Enter."}
