{"type": "thinking", "text": "With Auto-format OFF, Replace results in \"(A)  rent\\n\" — NO extra line! So the extra date/newline is caused by Auto-format firing as part of the Replace action. Specifically, the Replace action probably sends an Enter key to the editor (or triggers the IME action), which with Auto-format ON inserts a date on the blank current line (todo auto-format). With auto-format OFF, no newline appears at all. Interesting: so the replace action itself doesn't insert newline; the extra date is from auto-format's Enter handling triggered by the replace action? But with auto-format off, pressing Enter produced a newline, yet replace didn't add newline. Hmm, so the replace doesn't send Enter in the off case. Maybe the replace action calls \"format\" on the line which auto-format interprets by adding date? Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the mechanism: the replace action performs the text replacement via the editor's **\"replace text\" command**, then calls the auto-format logic which for todo.txt appends the date (as if a new task was entered) when the line ends with...? Hmm.\n\nWait, with auto-format ON, replace \"Pay\"→\"\" gave \"(A)  rent\\n2026-11-14 \". With auto-format OFF, replace gave \"(A)  rent\\n\". So the extra date is produced by **Auto-format** processing after the replace. So the bug could be attributed to \"Auto-format\" typing helper being applied incorrectly during search/replace. That ties to changed area #2! But what exactly is the expected behavior of Auto-format? In Markor, auto-format presumably reformats text as you type (indent lists etc.), not append dates. The date append on Enter in todo.txt might be an auto-format feature... but appending date on Enter to a blank line and to replace is odd.\n\nHmm, hold on: maybe the date insertion on Enter is actually a **\"typing helper\"** that is supposed to be OFF by default? The task says \"Editor overflow menu typing helpers: their toggles are now applied directly to the open editor session.\" Maybe \"Auto-format\" is one of the typing helpers, and the change was that toggling it applies live. The observed behavior (auto-format adds date in todo) might be pre-existing intentional behavior (Markor's todo auto-format adds a date when you insert a new task? maybe). But the search/replace dialog's Replace uses the editor's text-insertion API which triggers auto-format, adding a date — that's the bug from the shared layout (the Replace action incorrectly triggers auto-format/date insertion). Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the actual mechanism for the extra date is entirely different: The Search/Replace dialog's \"Replace\" calls `editor.replaceText` which triggers the todo **\"auto-format\"** listener on text change, and the auto-format adds a date because it thinks a new task line was created. Either way, it's a bug in the replace dialog (unwanted content).\n\nBut to make the report reproducible regardless of auto-format setting, better to mention with default settings (auto-format ON). But the developer might have auto-format off? Default is ON. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the reason the developer couldn't reproduce is that they don't have the Search/Replace dialog with empty replace? But we reproduced with \"Pay\"→\"Fee\" too. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the developer's \"could not reproduce\" is because they expect the repro to happen in the *in-editor find/replace dialog* (which works correctly). Since the task mentions \"Search and replace dialog: the input fields are now built from a shared layout\", the intended dialog may be the **in-editor replace bar** (searchEditText/replaceEditText) — and the injected bug might be there, not the todo popup. But I found the todo popup bug. The developer might have dismissed because steps didn't match their code area.\n\nHmm, let me think about the in-editor find/replace bar: We tested simple replace and regex replace, both worked. What about the \"shared layout\" bug: maybe the replace field's **input type / hint** is incorrect on rotation or when reopening? Or the fields lose content on rotate? Let's test rotation with the find/replace open — the task says test device rotation. Maybe the bug: rotating while the find/replace bar is open loses the input fields or the dialog. That's plausible for a \"shared layout\" issue. Let's test later.\n\nAlso test: open find/replace, type values, rotate, check still there. That's a good QA step.\n\nSimilarly for the Search/Replace popup: rotate while dialog open? The dialog would recreate; check fields. Hmm.\n\nGiven the developer rejection, maybe I should focus on the in-editor find/replace area for the shared-layout bug. But there might be no bug there. The date bug is real though; I can re-file with better evidence later.\n\nNow, the \"Auto-format\" toggle applied live: we observed that toggling it off changed Enter behavior immediately (date no longer added) — so the toggle applies to the open session. That's the changed feature working. Hmm, but maybe the expected default behavior of auto-format date insertion IS the bug? No.\n\nWait, actually maybe I mis-attributed. When Auto-format was ON and I pressed Enter, a date appeared. Is that expected? Markor's todo.txt auto-format might insert the current date when you press Enter on a task line, as a convenience for logging? Hmm, but it inserted the date on the current empty line, not new. Actually with auto-format ON, Enter inserts a new line and **the date is inserted at the start of the new line** (cursor after date). Wait, the text was \"(A) Pay rent\\n2026-11-14 \\n\" with cursor after \"2026-11-14 \" on line 2? The EditText text shows line 2 = \"2026-11-14 \", line 3 = \"\". Cursor at line 2? Actually the cursor position after Enter: the text ends with \"\\n\" so cursor is at end = line 3 start. Hmm, line 2 has date. So Enter inserted \"\\n2026-11-14 \\n\"? So date on line 2 and cursor line 3.\n\nThis looks like auto-format behavior: when pressing Enter in a todo.txt line, it might create a new line and add the current date as a \"completion date\" template? Hmm.\n\nWhatever—the key finding for area #2: toggling Auto-format off applied directly to open session (Enter no longer adds date; before, date added). That's the feature working, not a bug.\n\nSo area #2 might have another bug. Maybe the \"typing helpers\" are different toggles. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the File Settings menu — maybe the \"typing helpers\" are the items **\"Wrap Words\"**, **\"Line Numbers\"**, **\"Syntax Highlighting\"**, **\"Auto-format\"**. We tested all four apply live? Line numbers ✓, syntax highlighting ✓, auto-format ✓ (behavior changed). Wrap words not tested but likely. So area #2 seems fine.\n\nHmm, but then why mention \"typing helpers\" specifically? Maybe the UI label \"Auto-format\" is what they call a typing helper. Fine.\n\nNow, restore Auto-format ON (default) and undo the replace. Then re-enable? Let's do undo (38), then open overflow File Settings and toggle Auto-format back on. Also restore todo text.\n\nTap undo (38)."}
